My solution is ...
possible spoiler of course

or it might be a bug in the implementation

I use ^C ( or whatever your system uses to send a BREAK to the game )
which results in a "Really Quit (y/n) ?" prompt. Answer "n" and you are
awake and ready to fight some more.

On level 1 in discovery mode, using a blessed scroll of create monster
to get a floating eye after seeing a jackal ready to attack. My cat is
called WUSS.

WUSS misses the floating eye.  The jackal bites!--More---Really quit? [yn]n
{ top line is now clear, you are not paralyzed anymore but miss a turn }
WUSS bites the floating eye.  The jackal bites!
You miss the jackal.  WUSS bites the floating eye.  The jackal misses.
You miss the jackal.  WUSS misses the floating eye.  The jackal bites!
You hit the jackal. WUSS missed the floating. The jackal misses.
You destroy the jackal!  WUSS misses the floating eye.

The ^C method also works in early aborting of prayers when fighting monsters.
You pray, get full hits, then ^C to get out of prayer and continue hacking
the monsters. You don't have to wait for "You have finished your prayer."
The message still shows up but usually long after you have finished off the
monster and are on your merry way.

If your system does not support cooked input (IBM, AMIGA etc) this may not
work.

